sequenceDiagram
  participant K as Kiosk (installed web application)
  participant I as Device storage (IndexedDB)
  participant A as API (Express)
  participant F as Face service (Python)
  participant D as PostgreSQL
  Note over K,A: Before the outage (online)
  K->>A: GET /face/challenges (150 signed challenges, valid 72 h)
  A-->>K: signed two-step challenges
  K->>I: store the challenge pool and the kiosk session
  Note over K,I: During the outage (no internet)
  K->>K: capture 11 frames with a pooled challenge
  K->>I: store the capture encrypted (AES-GCM) with its original time
  K-->>K: saved, it will be verified when the connection returns
  Note over K,D: When the connection returns
  K->>A: POST /face/sync (up to 5 captures, device time)
  A->>A: check signature, validity window, single use, clock drift
  A->>F: POST /process (frames, challenge, layout)
  F-->>A: embedding and liveness result
  A->>D: match with the encrypted vectors of this school
  alt verified and no flag
    A->>D: insert the attendance event with the original capture time
  else doubtful
    A->>D: keep the capture encrypted for the principal's review
  end
  A-->>K: result for each capture
  K->>I: delete the synced captures
